{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fa2938c365cfcecc2e2fe645b0c737e7d4fc30b6ae61666b58ed501073bcdb8f","digest":{"component_or_area":"bug lifecycle and dependency linking","key_entities":["src/rebar/metrics/blame.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","src/rebar/_links.py","_write_link_event","caused_by","--caused-by","file_impact","rebar-ticket:","extract_ticket_refs","graph._links.add_dependency","docs/user-guide.md","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_caused_by_autoderive.py","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_caused_by_autoderive_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["blame-based causation","auto-derivation","caused_by link","culprit resolution","git blame","bug close","ticket trailer parsing"],"propositions":["On bug close, auto-derive a caused_by link by identifying the single dominant culprit commit (>50% of blamed lines) via git blame on the pre-fix state and resolving its rebar-ticket: trailer to a ticket.","The --caused-by <id> parameter allows explicit override or augmentation of the auto-derived culprit link at close time.","The auto-link must write via _write_link_event directly to bypass the closed-source guard, since the bug is already closed when auto-derivation runs.","No caused_by link is created when blame is ambiguous (no file_impact, no fixing commit, no >50% dominant commit, or no resolvable trailer).","The transition() library facade must thread the caused_by parameter end-to-end to support library callers, mirroring the --class threading pattern from ed13."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGE